  "notes": "Official cause code was reported as TBD/provisional on FORM-366; narrative attributes root cause to vendor dedication lubrication process deficiency, not an official NRC cause-code category (A-E). No previous similar events cited (narrative states 'None'), so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER emitted. Both inner and outer airlock equalizing valves are same model/manufacturer (Parker/Schrader M096-818-05, dedicated by Trentec) and failed by the same mechanism, but only the outer valve's gross leakage during LLRT caused the reportable inoperability; inner valve failure is noted as a contributing/related condition. 10 CFR 21.2(c) reporting captured as an additional regulatory reference alongside the two 50.73 criteria."
